    "method": "Convex hull (monotone chain) in EPSG:32630. Encloses 139230.0 m² across 498 m at its widest. A hull far longer than it is wide is a line the projection did not quite flatten, and should be read as one. A hull is convex. A distribution that is not — cases along a river, facilities along a coast — is filled in, so the hull asserts area where nothing was observed. It is an outline of what was observed, not a service area, a catchment or a boundary anyone agreed to.",
    "semantics": "A hull is an outline of what was observed, not a service area or a boundary anyone agreed to. It is convex, so a distribution that is not -- cases along a river -- is filled in, and the hull asserts area where nothing was observed."
